Assistant: You can use the dir(), gettys(), and remove() methods of the DirectoryInfo class, and their individual parameters to select and delete files and remove files.  But since you didn't specify what you actually wanted to do, I'm going to just give you an example of how to delete multiple files.  Here's a script that deletes everything in a directory but the last 10 files:

```
using System;
using System.IO;

namespace DeleteFilesDirectory
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            DirectoryInfo directory = new DirectoryInfo(@"C:\example\");

            foreach (FileInfo file in directory.GetFiles())
            {
                file.Delete();
            }

            directory = null;
        }
    }
}

